        <xs:element ref="RFI" minOccurs="0">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>A request for information (RFI) is a workflow where one or more issues or questions can be answered by different project participants.</xs:documentation>
            <xs:documentation>An RFI is a line item based document.  That is, it has a header for the RFI workflow and a flat list of line items.</xs:documentation>
            <xs:documentation>Each line item represents either an issue or a reply to an issue.  Issues and replies can be related to each other, but line items within an RFI are layed out linearly rather than nesting them.</xs:documentation>
            <xs:documentation>In its simplest form, an RFI has 2 line items:  one reply to one issue.  More generally, though, an issue can split into sub-issues, and strictly speaking, there is no restriction for a single top level issue.</xs:documentation>
            <xs:documentation>In addition, a line item is not limited to a single reply.  Rather, collaborative workflows could multiple participants contribute separate replies that then, optionally, feed into a final reply.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>